window.WORK_ITEMS = {"_comment":"COMMITTED. The two tracks of work for this project. Each item: {id, title, status(planned|active|done|blocked), start, updated, outcome, overview?, sessions[], researchRef?, reportRef?, reportHtml?}. `outcome` = one-line result (markdown spans OK). `overview` = a short markdown summary shown at the top of the detail view. `sessions` = agent-session ids (appended automatically by classify_session.mjs — additive; hand-edits preserved). `researchRef` (research track) points a round at a data/*.json research report. `reportRef` = a repo-relative .md file whose contents build_portal_data.mjs inlines (as reportMd) and the portal renders as a rich report. Files created/changed are derived automatically from each session's tool calls. NOTE: this file is hand-maintained — when a new unit of work happens, add/update an item here so the portal reflects it (the hook regenerates the portal FROM this file but never invents items).","tracks":{"build":{"label":"Build Tasks","items":[{"id":"build-command-center","title":"Stand up the AI Command Center for this project","status":"done","start":"2026-06-10","updated":"2026-06-10","outcome":"Reused the `meeting_ai` harness verbatim; `PROJECT_DIR` → `projects/agentforce-hackathon`; all prior contextual data reset to empty; authored fresh `GOALS.md` / `portal.json` / `work-items.json`.","overview":"Lifted the **reusable AI Command Center** (generic portal shell, scripts, hooks, subagents, secret-guard) from the prior `meeting_ai` project and repurposed it for the Agentforce Hackathon — without disturbing the existing SFDX project (`force-app/`, `.agents/skills/`, manifests).\n\n- **Verbatim harness:** `index.html`, `HARNESS.md`, all `command-center/scripts/*.mjs`, `.claude/` agents + `refresh-history` skill (byte-identical verified).\n- **One-line repurpose:** `PROJECT_DIR` in `session_lib.mjs` → `projects/agentforce-hackathon`.\n- **Empty contextual data:** fresh `sessions/index.json` (`[]`), `versions.json` (`[]`), `research.json` (pending); keyless `.env.example`. No meeting_ai content carried over.\n- **Fresh project content:** `GOALS.md`, root + project `AGENTS.md` (Salesforce-aware, points at `.agents/skills/`), `CLAUDE.md`, `portal.json`, this `work-items.json`.","sessions":[]},{"id":"build-plan-from-docs","title":"Read the Google Docs + clone the web-app; sharpen the plan","status":"done","start":"2026-06-10","updated":"2026-06-10","outcome":"Pulled the planning doc + the workshop setup-guide (via the Google Workspace MCP) and vendored the reference web app into `web-app/`. **Use case, deployment, and flow are now concrete** — GOALS.md updated.","overview":"Ingested two Google Docs and a reference repo, then re-grounded the plan on real decisions:\n\n- **Use case = Employee Agent V1** (meeting-note agent: ingest notes/transcript → log to a Notes record, summarize, create tasks, draft email). Maps to the `Note_taking_agent` already in `force-app/`.\n- **Deployment = package-based** (install link), **not** browser-OAuth — a firm decision to avoid security warnings / participant anxiety. `AiAuthoringBundle` still isn't packageable, so the package ships everything *around* the agent and the attendee builds it in Agent Studio.\n- **Workshop flow (decided):** Part A guided (instructions → add Note + Summarize actions → preview → commit → test) + Part B free exercise (draft email, Query Records, Search Web, fetch tasks, image/voice).\n- **Backup = a free pre-configured org** for anyone whose primary org fails.\n- **Web app** vendored into `web-app/` from `flemx/vibe-code-agenforce-claude` (Vite+React; content in `MainContent.jsx`) — to be re-scripted to our flow (see `web-app/NOTES.md`).","sessions":[]},{"id":"build-package-assets","title":"Lightning app + LWC launchpad + unlocked package (G1/G2/G3)","status":"done","start":"2026-06-10","updated":"2026-06-11","outcome":"Shipped as an **unlocked package** (`Employee Agent Workshop 0.1.0.1`, `04tWt000000GDJ3IAO`) built from the `hackathon` DevHub and **installed + browser-verified in `hackathon_sandbox`**: the app loads, **Run Setup** assigns all perm sets, the launchpad shows \"Setup complete.\" Fixed three real bugs found via agent-browser (missing tab, broken `AFDX_User_Perms` group, namespaced perm-set lookup) and removed scaffold junk. All **13 Apex tests pass**.","overview":"The starting point of the workshop — what the install lands in. **Package-based by decision** (avoids browser-OAuth security warnings); ships everything *around* the agent (the agent is built in-org because `AiAuthoringBundle` isn't packageable).\n\n**Built this session:**\n- **`Employee_Agent_Workshop` Lightning app** + **`Employee_Agent_Workshop_Home`** App-page (FlexiPage) + tab — the launchpad surface.\n- **`workshopLaunchpad` LWC** — welcome hero, **Open the workshop guide** link, and a **Run Setup** button with live per-item status (SLDS, accessible, idempotent re-runs).\n- **`WorkshopSetupController`** (`@AuraEnabled`) — assigns the configured permission sets / groups to `UserInfo.getUserId()` idempotently with partial-success DML; **setup-object DML only, so no mixed-DML risk** (validated by the feasibility research). Built-in Apex defaults (`Employee_Agent_Workshop` PS + `AFDX_User_Perms` PSG + `Note_taking_agent`) so it works on a clean install with **no** custom-metadata record.\n- **`Workshop_Settings__mdt`** type (5 fields) as an **optional point-and-click override** for the guide/install URLs.\n- **`Employee_Agent_Workshop`** permission set (package-safe: no `agentAccesses` to the not-yet-built agent).\n\n**Gotcha found & worked around:** deploying a Custom Metadata *record with values* via the CLI throws an opaque `UNKNOWN_EXCEPTION` on these orgs (reproduces for a brand-new throwaway CMDT type; a skeleton record with no values deploys fine). Fix: real defaults live in **Apex**, the record is an optional Setup-edited override moved to `docs/optional-metadata/` so a full-source deploy / package build never breaks.\n\n**Packaged & browser-tested (2026-06-11):** decided **unlocked package**, built `Employee Agent Workshop 0.1.0.1` (`04tWt000000GDJ3IAO`) from the `hackathon` DevHub and installed it into `hackathon_sandbox`. Tested the running app with **agent-browser** and fixed three real bugs: (1) the **Home tab** had been rolled back by an earlier failed multi-component deploy + the perm set lacked tab visibility → redeployed the tab and added `tabSettings`; (2) **Run Setup** referenced the broken scaffold group `AFDX_User_Perms` → switched to assigning the **standard OOB perm sets** (`force__EinsteinGPTPromptTemplateUser`, `force__CopilotSalesforceUser`) + `Employee_Agent_Workshop`; (3) **namespaced perm-set lookup** (`WHERE Name='force__…'` matched nothing) → strip/rederive the namespace. Removed scaffold junk (`Resort_*`, `AFDX_*`, weather Apex, `Get_Event_Info`, `Get_Resort_Hours`, `Local_Info_Agent`) and `.forceignore`d `aiAuthoringBundles`. Verified end-to-end in the sandbox: app loads, Run Setup → all perms assigned, accelerator → agent published+activated.\n\n**Next:** the action assets (Note Flow + Summarize prompt template) in the asset library; finalize the agent starter; set the real guide/install URLs.","sessions":[]},{"id":"build-agent-deploy-accelerator","title":"Browser-side agent deploy accelerator (NGA Connect API) — stretch G2","status":"done","start":"2026-06-11","updated":"2026-06-11","outcome":"Proved — and shipped — a one-click **deploy → publish → activate** of the Agent Script agent from the browser, using the internal **Next-Gen Authoring Connect API**. End-to-end verified live on `hackathon_sb` (Bot created + activated) via the `NextGenAgentDeployer` Apex; **12/12 tests pass**, deployer coverage 86%.","overview":"The stretch accelerator from G2, now real. `AiAuthoringBundle` can't be packaged and `sf agent publish` is CLI-only — but the internal **Next-Gen Authoring Connect API** (`/services/data/v64.0/nextgen-authoring/...`, found via code search of the OpenAPI spec) lets us do it from an in-org callout.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **`NextGenAgentDeployer`** (Apex) reads the Agent Script from a **Static Resource** (`Note_taking_agent_afscript`), rewrites its `developer_name`/`agent_label` to the requested apiName, then calls **create → publish → activate** and assigns the agent-access perm set — all server-side.\n- **`NextGenAgentDeployerSession`** (Visualforce, `{!$Api.Session_ID}`) supplies an **API-enabled session** (the Lightning/LWC session isn't reliably API-enabled; a self-callout to the org My Domain needs no Remote Site Setting).\n- **`agentDeployButton`** LWC — an *optional, clearly-marked* \"deploy the agent for me\" button on the launchpad Home page (for the backup org / stuck attendees; the main path is still build-it-in-Studio).\n\n**Gotchas found & fixed (see `docs/reference/nextgen-authoring-connect-api.md`):** live path has **no `/connect/`** segment; the runtime BotDefinition name comes from `developer_name` *inside* the afscript (collision → `DUPLICATE_VALUE`, fixed by rewriting it); activate returns 204; published agents can't be fully API-deleted.\n\n**Decision:** ship it as an internal accelerator, NOT the customer happy-path — the endpoint is undocumented (fragile) and auto-publishing would remove Part A's learning.","reportRef":"docs/reference/nextgen-authoring-connect-api.md","sessions":[],"reportMd":"# Next-Gen Authoring Connect API — agent deploy/publish from the browser\n\n> Source of truth: the internal OpenAPI spec\n> `core/next-gen-authoring-connect-api/java/resources/authoring-bundle-connect-api-spec.yaml`\n> (found via code search in `gitcore.soma.salesforce.com/core-2206/core-264-public`).\n> This is the API the new Agent Builder UI uses. It is **internal/undocumented** — use it for\n> our own accelerator, not as a customer-facing contract (it can change without notice).\n\n## Why this matters\n`AiAuthoringBundle` can't be packaged, and `sf agent publish` is CLI-only — but this Connect API\n**does** let us create → publish → activate an Agent Script agent entirely from an in-org callout.\nThat powers the optional **\"deploy the agent for me\"** accelerator (`NextGenAgentDeployer`).\n\n## Base path (verified live on hackathon_sb)\n```\n/services/data/v64.0/nextgen-authoring        ← NOTE: no /connect/ segment\n```\nA `GET .../nextgen-authoring/bundles` returns the org's bundles. (The `/connect/` variant 404s.)\n\n## Endpoints we use\n| Step | Method + path | Body | Returns |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Create | `POST /bundles` | `{apiName,label,assets:[{resourceName,resourceContent,resourceType:\"agentDefinition\",resourceAuthoringFormat:\"afscript\",authoringFormatVersion:\"v1.0\"}]}` | `{id (=bundleVersionId), bundleId, apiName, versionStatus:\"DRAFT\"}` |\n| Publish | `POST /bundle-versions/{bundleVersionId}/publish` | `{}` | `201 {publishedBotId, publishedBotVersionId, lastPublishedOn}` |\n| Activate | `POST /bundle-versions/{bundleVersionId}/activate` | `{}` | `204` (no content) |\n| Deactivate | `POST /bundle-versions/{bundleVersionId}/deactivate` | `{}` | `204` |\n| List | `GET /bundles` | — | `{bundles:[{id,apiName,latestBundleVersionId,activeBundleVersionId,...}]}` |\n| Compile | `POST /afscript/compile` | `{content, bundleVersionId?}` (text/plain) | compile result + errors |\n| Validate | `POST /bundle-versions/{id}/validate` | `{agentJsonString}` | compile/validation result |\n\nOther endpoints in the spec: create draft (`/draft`), versions list (`/bundles/{id}/versions`),\nversion detail (`GET /bundle-versions/{id}`), summary, version-info, migrate, delete.\n\nAccess gate (from the spec's `static-access-check`):\n`NextGenAuthoring.orgHasNextGenAgentAuthoringEnabled && userCanAccessNextGenAgentAuthoring`.\n\n## Hard-won gotchas (verified 2026-06-11)\n1. **Session must be API-enabled.** A self-callout to `URL.getOrgDomainUrl()` works from Apex with\n   `UserInfo.getSessionId()` in *anonymous* and *Visualforce* contexts. In an **Aura/LWC** request\n   the session may NOT be API-enabled — so the accelerator runs the callout server-side in Apex and\n   sources the session from a **Visualforce page** (`NextGenAgentDeployerSession`,\n   `{!$Api.Session_ID}`). No Remote Site Setting is needed for the org's own My Domain.\n2. **`developer_name` inside the afscript = the runtime BotDefinition name.** It is NOT taken from\n   the bundle `apiName`. If two bundles carry the same `developer_name`, publish fails with\n   `DUPLICATE_VALUE: BotDefinition duplicates value on record with id: <name>`. `NextGenAgentDeployer`\n   rewrites `developer_name`/`agent_label` in the script to match the requested apiName before create.\n3. **Publish/activate bodies:** send `{}` (an empty/again-missing body can be silently dropped by some\n   clients; `sf api request rest --body @file` with `{}` works). Activate returns **204** (no JSON).\n4. **Published agents can't be fully deleted** via the API (BotDefinition lingers) — same as the CLI.\n   Use unique throwaway names when testing; clean up via Setup or scratch-org expiry.\n\n## Round-trip proven on hackathon_sb\n`create → publish (201, Bot+BotVersion created) → activate (204) → versionStatus PUBLISHED /\ntargetStatus ACTIVE`, with the BotDefinition visible via SOQL — both via raw REST and via the\n`NextGenAgentDeployer` Apex class (`ZZ_Workshop_Live_01`).\n"},{"id":"build-note-capture-suite","title":"Note-capture suite: audio/file/text → agent, HTML notes, note viewer","status":"done","start":"2026-06-11","updated":"2026-06-11","outcome":"Built & sandbox-verified 4 components: **noteCapture** LWC (record audio → speech-to-text, drag files → image-to-text via prompt template, paste text → send to a chosen Employee Agent via the ACC API), **HtmlNoteService** (richly-formatted ContentNote from HTML, 8/8 tests), **noteViewer** LWC + controller (read-only HTML render + Download-PDF, 3/3), and the **NoteCaptureController/AI** backends (4/4 each). All 27 Apex tests pass; the HTML-note round-trip is verified live.","overview":"A richer capture + notes experience around the agent.\n\n- **`noteCapture` LWC** — three input paths (animated audio recorder → `convertBase64SpeechToText`; multi-file drag → multimodal prompt template `ConnectApi.EinsteinLLM.generateMessagesForPromptTemplate`, parallel; pasted text), combined and sent to a chosen Employee Agent via `lightning/accApi` (open + execute).\n- **`HtmlNoteService`** (Apex + `@InvocableMethod`) — creates a formatted `ContentNote` (HTML in a Blob, sanitized to an allowed-tag whitelist), links to a record. Unlocks polished meeting summaries + a workshop-report deliverable.\n- **`noteViewer` LWC + `NoteViewerController`** — lists notes, renders HTML read-only via `lightning-formatted-rich-text`, Download-PDF via a print window.\n- **Backends:** `NoteCaptureController` (ContentVersion upload, Employee-Agent listing), `NoteCaptureAI` (speech-to-text + prompt template, graceful degradation when AI is off).\n\n**Packaging decision:** these depend on org features (`ContentNote`, `ConnectApi.EinsteinLLM`, `BotDefinition`) absent from the vanilla 2GP build org, so they're kept in **`feature-addons/`** and deployed directly (own `Employee_Agent_Notes_Addon` perm set) — the core package stays clean. Verified end-to-end in `hackathon_sandbox`; report at `docs/component-test-report.html`.","reportRef":"docs/component-test-report.html","sessions":[],"reportMd":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\"/>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"/>\n<title>Note-Capture Components — Test Report</title>\n<style>\n  :root{--bg:#0a0a14;--card:#15152a;--card2:#1c1c36;--border:#2e2e4a;--text:#f4f4f8;--muted:#a3a3b8;\n    --accent:#7c3aed;--accent2:#a78bfa;--green:#34d399;--amber:#fbbf24;--blue:#38bdf8;--red:#f87171;}\n  *{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0;}\n  body{font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\n    background:radial-gradient(circle at 15% 8%,rgba(124,58,237,.22)0%,transparent 45%),\n    radial-gradient(circle at 85% 92%,rgba(56,189,248,.13)0%,transparent 45%),var(--bg);color:var(--text);line-height:1.6;}\n  .wrap{max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:46px 24px 90px;}\n  header.hero{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:34px 38px;\n    background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(124,58,237,.18),rgba(28,28,54,.6));box-shadow:0 12px 40px rgba(0,0,0,.45);}\n  .eyebrow{text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.18em;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent2);margin-bottom:10px;}\n  h1{font-size:30px;line-height:1.18;margin-bottom:12px;}\n  .hero p{color:var(--muted);font-size:16px;max-width:74ch;}\n  .chips{margin-top:18px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:9px;}\n  .chip{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;padding:6px 13px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid var(--border);\n    background:rgba(255,255,255,.03);color:var(--muted);}\n  .stats{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:15px;margin:26px 0 6px;}\n  .stat{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;padding:18px;background:var(--card);text-align:center;}\n  .stat .num{font-size:26px;font-weight:800;color:var(--accent2);}\n  .stat .lbl{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:3px;}\n  h2{font-size:21px;margin:46px 0 8px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;}\n  h2 .bar{width:4px;height:21px;border-radius:2px;background:linear-gradient(var(--accent),var(--accent2));}\n  .sub{color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:16px;font-size:14.5px;}\n  .card{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:16px;padding:22px 24px;background:var(--card);margin-bottom:16px;}\n  .card h3{font-size:17px;margin-bottom:8px;}\n  table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:6px;}\n  th,td{text-align:left;padding:9px 13px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);font-size:13.5px;vertical-align:top;}\n  th{color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;font-size:11.5px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;}\n  code{font-family:\"JetBrains Mono\",ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12px;background:var(--card2);\n    border:1px solid var(--border);padding:1.5px 6px;border-radius:5px;color:#d6c8ff;}\n  .s{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:5px;white-space:nowrap;}\n  .s.ok{background:rgba(52,211,153,.16);color:var(--green);}\n  .s.warn{background:rgba(251,191,36,.16);color:var(--amber);}\n  .shot{margin:14px 0;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#fff;}\n  .shot img{display:block;width:100%;}\n  .shot figcaption{background:var(--card2);color:var(--muted);font-size:12.5px;padding:8px 14px;border-top:1px solid var(--border);}\n  ul.clean{list-style:none;} ul.clean li{padding:5px 0 5px 24px;position:relative;}\n  ul.clean li::before{content:\"\\2713\";position:absolute;left:2px;top:5px;color:var(--green);font-weight:800;}\n  .callout{border-left:3px solid var(--amber);border-radius:10px;background:rgba(251,191,36,.08);padding:14px 18px;margin:14px 0;}\n  .callout p{margin:0;color:var(--muted);} .callout strong{color:var(--text);}\n  a{color:var(--accent2);}\n  footer{margin-top:40px;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;text-align:center;border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:20px;}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"wrap\">\n  <header class=\"hero\">\n    <p class=\"eyebrow\">Agentforce Workshop · Component Test Report</p>\n    <h1>Note-capture, HTML-note &amp; note-viewer components — built &amp; tested</h1>\n    <p>This documents the new components requested: capturing meeting notes (audio + files + text) and sending them to an agent, creating richly-formatted HTML notes, and a read-only note viewer with PDF download. All were deployed to the sandbox and verified in the browser.</p>\n    <div class=\"chips\">\n      <span class=\"chip\">📅 2026-06-11</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">🧪 hackathon_sandbox</span>\n      <span class=\"chip\">✅ 27/27 Apex tests passing</span>\n    </div>\n  </header>\n\n  <div class=\"stats\">\n    <div class=\"stat\"><div class=\"num\">4</div><div class=\"lbl\">new components</div></div>\n    <div class=\"stat\"><div class=\"num\">27/27</div><div class=\"lbl\">Apex tests pass</div></div>\n    <div class=\"stat\"><div class=\"num\">live</div><div class=\"lbl\">browser-verified</div></div>\n    <div class=\"stat\"><div class=\"num\">0.1.0.2</div><div class=\"lbl\">core package built</div></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- WHAT WAS BUILT -->\n  <h2><span class=\"bar\"></span>What was built</h2>\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <table>\n      <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Type</th><th>What it does</th><th>Tests</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td><code>noteCapture</code></td><td>LWC</td><td>Record audio (with animation) → speech-to-text; drag in multiple files → image/doc-to-text via prompt template (parallel); paste text. Combine + send to a chosen Employee Agent (ACC API).</td><td><span class=\"s ok\">via controllers</span></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><code>NoteCaptureController</code></td><td>Apex</td><td>Saves files as Salesforce Files (ContentVersion), lists Employee Agents to target.</td><td><span class=\"s ok\">4/4</span></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><code>NoteCaptureAI</code></td><td>Apex</td><td>Speech-to-text + multimodal prompt template invocation; degrades gracefully if AI features are off.</td><td><span class=\"s ok\">4/4</span></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><code>HtmlNoteService</code></td><td>Apex + Invocable</td><td>Creates a richly-formatted <code>ContentNote</code> from HTML (sanitized), links it to a record. Callable from LWC, Flow, or the agent.</td><td><span class=\"s ok\">8/8</span></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><code>noteViewer</code> + <code>NoteViewerController</code></td><td>LWC + Apex</td><td>Lists notes, renders the selected note's HTML read-only, Download-PDF (print) button.</td><td><span class=\"s ok\">3/3</span></td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- EVIDENCE -->\n  <h2><span class=\"bar\"></span>Tested in the browser — evidence</h2>\n  <p class=\"sub\">Captured live from the workshop Home page in <code>hackathon_sandbox</code>.</p>\n\n  <figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"screenshots/components/02-note-capture.png\" alt=\"Note capture component\"/>\n    <figcaption>Capture Meeting Notes — the audio recorder (big record button, \"Tap to record. Tap again to stop and transcribe\"), plus the numbered file-drop and paste-text steps.</figcaption></figure>\n\n  <figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"screenshots/components/04-send-to-agent.png\" alt=\"Send to agent\"/>\n    <figcaption>The capture flow: combine audio + files + text, then choose an Employee Agent and send (via the Agentforce client API).</figcaption></figure>\n\n  <figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"screenshots/components/03-note-viewer.png\" alt=\"HTML note viewer rendering formatted content\"/>\n    <figcaption>The note viewer rendering a real HTML note created by <code>HtmlNoteService</code> — headings, bold labels, bulleted &amp; numbered lists all render. A Download-PDF button is top-right. This proves the full round-trip: create HTML note → read it back → render formatted.</figcaption></figure>\n\n  <figure class=\"shot\"><img src=\"screenshots/components/01-home-all-components.png\" alt=\"All components on the workshop home\"/>\n    <figcaption>All components live together on the workshop Home page.</figcaption></figure>\n\n  <!-- HOW VERIFIED -->\n  <h2><span class=\"bar\"></span>How each was verified</h2>\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <ul class=\"clean\">\n      <li><strong>HTML note round-trip</strong> — created a formatted \"Meeting Notes — Acme Corp\" note via Apex; it rendered correctly in the viewer (screenshot above).</li>\n      <li><strong>HtmlNoteService</strong> — 8 Apex tests: create, link-to-record, idempotent link, blank-title rejection, invocable success + failure, HTML sanitization (script/disallowed tags stripped, allowed tags kept).</li>\n      <li><strong>NoteViewerController</strong> — 3 tests: fetch note HTML, list notes, default limit.</li>\n      <li><strong>NoteCaptureController</strong> — 4 tests: file upload, upload+link, blank rejection, agent listing.</li>\n      <li><strong>NoteCaptureAI</strong> — 4 tests via a mock seam (speech-to-text + prompt template), incl. graceful degradation when AI features are off.</li>\n      <li><strong>noteCapture / noteViewer LWCs</strong> — rendered live on the Home page; audio recorder UI, file drop, agent picker, and the formatted note view all display correctly.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- NOTES / DECISIONS -->\n  <h2><span class=\"bar\"></span>Key decisions &amp; honest caveats</h2>\n  <div class=\"card\">\n    <div class=\"callout\"><p><strong>Packaging split:</strong> these four components depend on org features (<code>ContentNote</code>, <code>ConnectApi.EinsteinLLM</code>, <code>BotDefinition</code>) that aren't present in the vanilla scratch org the 2GP package build uses — so they don't compile there. They're kept in a separate <code>feature-addons/</code> folder and deployed to the org directly (same pattern as the un-packageable agent). The <strong>core package (0.1.0.2)</strong> still builds &amp; installs cleanly. Deploy the add-ons with <code>sf project deploy start --source-dir feature-addons</code> + assign the <code>Employee_Agent_Notes_Addon</code> perm set. See <code>feature-addons/README.md</code>.</p></div>\n    <div class=\"callout\"><p><strong>Speech-to-text &amp; prompt-template calls:</strong> the actual AI calls (the <code>convertBase64SpeechToText</code> action and the multimodal prompt template) require those features enabled and configured in the org. The Apex compiles and the orchestration is tested; if a feature is off, the component shows a clear \"paste the text instead\" placeholder rather than failing. Live AI output should be verified once the org's prompt template (<code>Describe_File_Contents</code>) and speech action are confirmed available.</p></div>\n    <div class=\"callout\"><p><strong>Send-to-agent (ACC API):</strong> uses <code>lightning/accApi</code> (<code>open</code> + <code>execute</code>) to open the agent side panel and submit the notes. This works on Lightning desktop with Agentforce; elsewhere it falls back to a bubbling event. Worth a final manual click-through on a record page with an active agent.</p></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <footer>Generated 2026-06-11 · Note-capture component suite · sandbox-verified · core package 0.1.0.2 (04tWt000000GDXZIA4)</footer>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n"},{"id":"build-actions-library","title":"The actions library — Note + Summarize (+ free-exercise add-ons) (G4)","status":"planned","start":"2026-06-10","updated":"2026-06-10","outcome":"The supporting actions the agent uses: Log/Create Note (Flow), Summarize (Prompt Template), plus Query Records, draft email, fetch tasks, Search Web for the free exercise. OOB-first.","overview":"The agent's capabilities, shipped in the package's asset library so attendees just **add** them — no building from scratch.\n\n- **Part A (required):** **Log/Create Note** (Flow — already `First_Agent_Log_Account_Note`) + **Summarize** (Prompt Template).\n- **Part B (free exercise):** **Query Records** (find an account/case to associate), **draft follow-up email**, **fetch tasks** from notes, **Search Web**, Knowledge.\n- **Prefer out-of-the-box / standard actions.** Custom Apex only where it clearly adds value — e.g. an **HTML-note** action (Base64 for richer layouts) and a **SOSL record-search** action (dynamic find across objects). These two are owner action items from the planning doc.","sessions":[]},{"id":"build-webapp-script","title":"Re-script the workshop web app to our Employee-Agent-V1 flow (G5/G6)","status":"done","start":"2026-06-10","updated":"2026-06-11","outcome":"Re-scripted the vendored `web-app/` to **our** flow (5 sections), added a worked **Query Records** example, and **deployed it live to Heroku** (https://employee-agent-workshop-guide-3ae92a297614.herokuapp.com/) with the real package install URL. The guide URL is **wired into the Lightning app**. Agentforce Labs kept as the backup-org path.","overview":"The reused guide app at `web-app/` (Vite + React, from `flemx/vibe-code-agenforce-claude`) — **shell kept, content fully re-scripted** to the Employee Agent V1 workshop.\n\n**Done this session:**\n- **`MainContent.jsx`** rewritten — sections `overview` · `get-org` · `install-package` · `part-a` · `part-b`, each with right-sidebar step anchors. Part A mirrors Hanne's setup-guide doc verbatim (check basics → reasoning instructions → add **Log Note** + **Summarize** from the asset library → Preview → Commit → test on a record); Part B is the free exercise (draft email, adapt summary, fetch tasks, web search, voice/image, custom actions).\n- **Backup org:** the **Agentforce Labs** instructions are preserved as **Option 2 — the free backup org** (per request).\n- **Install URL:** a top-of-file **`PACKAGE_INSTALL_URL` placeholder** constant (+ `BACKUP_ORG_URL`) — one line to set before the event.\n- **`Sidebar.jsx`** nav + heading updated; **`index.html`** title/description updated; a `cta-button` style added to `index.css`. Production `vite build` succeeds.","reportRef":"web-app/NOTES.md","sessions":[],"reportMd":"# web-app/ — the self-guided workshop guide (Track B)\n\n## Provenance\nVendored from **https://github.com/flemx/vibe-code-agenforce-claude** (cloned 2026-06-10, `.git`\ndropped so it lives inside this repo). It's a clean **Vite 5 + React 18** single-page guide; **all\ncontent lives in `src/components/MainContent.jsx`**; deploys to Heroku (`Procfile` + `static.json` +\n`heroku-postbuild`). Authoring/deploy mechanics are documented in **`web-app/CLAUDE.md`** (kept as-is).\n\n## What it currently is vs. what we need\nThe reference app guides a **different** workshop — \"Vibe Code with Claude Code\": CLI auth → create an\nagent by prompting Claude Code (a *customer-service* agent). We are **reusing the shell, re-scripting the\ncontent** for **our** flow.\n\n## Our script (from the setup-guide doc + planning doc — see GOALS.md)\nUse case: **Employee Agent V1** — a meeting-note agent (ingest notes/transcript → log to a Notes record,\nsummarize, create tasks, draft email). Deployment is **package-based** (install link), not CLI/OAuth.\n\nRe-script `MainContent.jsx` sections to:\n1. **Overview** — what we're building + what's preconfigured (Foundations, perm sets, action assets, the\n   Employee Agent V1 framework).\n2. **Get an org** — primary path + the **free pre-configured backup org**.\n3. **Install the package** — the install link (replaces the reference app's CLI auth steps).\n4. **Part A — guided build (in Agent Studio):** open the agent → review basics → write **reasoning\n   instructions** → add **Create/Log Note** + **Summarize** actions from the asset library → **Preview**\n   → **Commit version** → verify the agent appears → test on a record.\n5. **Part B — free exercise:** draft email · adapt summary format · fetch tasks · **Query Records** ·\n   **Search Web** · image/voice via LWC · custom actions.\n\n## Re-script checklist (per web-app/CLAUDE.md)\n- `src/components/MainContent.jsx` — `sections` array, `sectionTitles`, per-section components, the\n  `steps` arrays for the right sidebar.\n- `src/components/Sidebar.jsx` — `navigationItems` + the heading/logo.\n- `src/App.jsx` — `pathToSection` / `sectionToPath` routing.\n- `index.html` — `<title>` + favicon.\n- `public/images/` — swap in our screenshots (the setup-guide doc has the Agent-Studio screenshots).\n\n## Status — re-scripted (2026-06-11)\nContent is now **our** flow. `MainContent.jsx` was rewritten to 5 sections — `overview` · `get-org` ·\n`install-package` · `part-a` · `part-b` — with right-sidebar step anchors. `Sidebar.jsx` (nav + heading)\nand `index.html` (title/description) updated; a `cta-button` style was added to `index.css`.\n`npm run build` passes.\n\n**Two placeholders to set before the event** (top of `MainContent.jsx`):\n- `PACKAGE_INSTALL_URL` — the supporting-assets package install link.\n- `BACKUP_ORG_URL` — currently Agentforce Labs (`https://labs.agentforce.com/`), the backup-org path.\n\n**Still to do:** swap `public/images/` for the real Agent-Studio screenshots from the setup-guide doc\n(a few reference images are reused as placeholders), and deploy to Heroku (see `web-app/CLAUDE.md`).\n"},{"id":"build-backup-org","title":"Free pre-configured backup org (G6)","status":"planned","start":"2026-06-10","updated":"2026-06-10","outcome":"A free, pre-configured org handed to any attendee whose own org won't cooperate — provisioned and documented so it never derails the room.","overview":"Decided in the planning doc: provide a **free, pre-configured backup org** as the room's safety net (flaky Wi-Fi, provisioning failures, mixed skill levels). Define how it's provisioned (Agentforce enabled, package pre-installed, perms assigned), how an attendee is handed one mid-session, and document the handoff in the web app's org step.","sessions":[]}]},"research":{"label":"Research Rounds","items":[{"id":"research-packaging-and-deploy","title":"What's packageable for Agentforce + browser-side deploy / perm-assignment path","status":"done","start":"2026-06-10","updated":"2026-06-11","outcome":"**Confirmed:** perm-set assignment from `@AuraEnabled` Apex is the reliable browser-triggered path (setup-object DML only → no mixed-DML); **runtime publish of the `AiAuthoringBundle` from the browser is NOT viable** — publishing is CLI/Studio-only (no Apex/REST entry point), and `UserInfo.getSessionId()` is intentionally not API-enabled in Lightning. So: LWC button does perm-set assignment; attendee builds the agent in Agent Studio.","overview":"Source-cited feasibility investigation (background subagent, 2026-06-11) into doing config/deploy **from the browser**:\n\n- **Perm-set assignment (✅ green light):** `Database.insert(new PermissionSetAssignment(AssigneeId=UserInfo.getUserId(), PermissionSetId=…))` from `@AuraEnabled` Apex; look up by `Name` (PS) / `DeveloperName` (PSG); idempotent by checking existing assignments; **no mixed-DML** as long as only setup-object DML runs in the transaction (HIGH confidence).\n- **Runtime `AiAuthoringBundle` deploy/publish (❌ not viable):** publishing an Agent Script bundle is a CLI/Studio-only compile step (`sf agent publish`) with no public Apex/REST endpoint; the MD-API-from-Apex path is blocked because the Lightning-context `UserInfo.getSessionId()` is deliberately **not** API-enabled (Visualforce-page session is the only workaround). Deploying the bundle *source* only stages a DRAFT — it doesn't create the live Bot/BotVersion.\n- **What IS packageable:** perm sets/groups (incl. `agentAccesses`), Apex, Flows, `GenAiPromptTemplate`, Lightning app + Home page + LWC, custom objects/fields, and `BotTemplate` (Bot-based agents). **NOT** `AiAuthoringBundle`.\n- **Net:** the package ships supporting assets; the LWC launchpad assigns perms; the attendee builds & publishes Employee Agent V1 in Agent Studio. (Optionally auto-activate a published BotVersion via the Connect REST `bot-versions/{id}/activation` endpoint, server-side.)\n\nThis directly validated the **`build-package-assets`** architecture.","sessions":[]}]}}};
